  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — Canon Web\n\n**Current state: zero test coverage.** No test runner is installed (`package.json` has no `vitest`/`jest`, no `test` script), and there are no `*.test.ts(x)` or `*.spec.ts(x)` files anywhere in the repo. Every function below is therefore untested by definition — I'm prioritizing by risk/value rather than listing all ~100 files.\n\n### 0. Setup needed first\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jsdom\n```\nAdd to `package.json`: `\"test\": \"vitest\"`. Pure-logic files (`lib/*.ts`, `types/*.ts`) need no DOM; `lib/server/*.ts` needs a Postgres test instance or a mocked `getDb()` (Drizzle supports `drizzle-orm/pg-core` test doubles, or use `pglite`/testcontainers).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pure logic — highest value, zero setup cost\n\n### `lib/validate-value.ts` — `foldValue`, `checkObservedValue` (untested, security-relevant: this is the anti-hallucination guard)\n\nGaps: suffix-stripping order (`\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\"` → double suffix), suffix-as-whole-value edge case (`folded === suffix` guard, e.g. value is literally `\"Inc\"`), Unicode normalization (NFKD), empty/whitespace-only candidate, candidate matching via fold but not exact, both sides empty (orphan case), duplicate values in `observed`.\n\n```ts\n// lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue } from \"./validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"folds case, punctuation and whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(foldValue(\"ACME INC\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips a single legal suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme Corp\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips multiple stacked suffixes, longest first\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not strip a suffix that is the entire value\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Inc\")).toBe(\"inc\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"is total and deterministic for repeated calls\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ünïcödé Co.\")).toBe(foldValue(\"Ünïcödé Co.\"));\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"  \", [\"Acme\"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects when neither side has a value (orphan)\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"Acme\", [\"\", \"  \"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"Acme Inc\", [\"Acme Inc\", \"ACME INC\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Inc\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts a folded-equivalent match and returns the observed form\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"acme inc.\", [\"Acme Inc\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Inc\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a value that is neither observed nor a legal normalization\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACC-9999\", [\"ACC-1\", \"ACC-2\"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/diff-chars.ts` — `diffSegments`\n\nGaps: equal strings, completely disjoint strings, one empty string, overlapping prefix/suffix windows (e.g. `\"aa\"` vs `\"a\"` — must not double-count), one string a substring of the other.\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { diffSegments } from \"./diff-chars\";\n\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"returns everything as prefix when equal\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"finds a middle-only diff\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\")).toEqual({\n      prefix: \"ACC-\", middle: \"4417\", suffix: \"\",\n    });\n  });\n\n  it(\"finds a shared suffix\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC-SOUTH\")).toEqual({\n      prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"-SOUTH\",\n    });\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles one empty string\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"\", \"Acme\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"Acme\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not double-count overlapping prefix/suffix windows\", () => {\n    // max=1 (shorter string length); prefix and suffix scans must not exceed it\n    expect(diffSegments(\"aa\", \"a\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"a\", middle: \"a\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/format.ts` — six formatters, all untested\n\nGaps: `shortRunId` with a non-hyphenated / short id; `formatElapsed` at exact minute/hour boundaries and negative input; `formatStat`/`formatCount` with `0` vs `null` vs `undefined` (the whole point of the function); `formatRelative` boundary seconds (59s/60s, 23h/24h); `formatConfidence` rounding (e.g. `0.855`).\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { shortRunId, formatElapsed, formatStat, formatRelative, formatConfidence } from \"./format\";\n\ndescribe(\"formatElapsed\", () => {\n  it(\"clamps negative ms to zero\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(-500)).toBe(\"00:00\");\n  });\n  it(\"rolls to h:mm:ss past one hour\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(3_661_000)).toBe(\"1:01:01\");\n  });\n  it(\"stays mm:ss under an hour\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(59_000)).toBe(\"00:59\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatStat\", () => {\n  it(\"renders 0 as a number, not a dash\", () => {\n    expect(formatStat(0)).toBe(\"0\");\n  });\n  it(\"renders null/undefined as an em dash\", () => {\n    expect(formatStat(null)).toBe(\"—\");\n    expect(formatStat(undefined)).toBe(\"—\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatRelative\", () => {\n  it(\"says 'just now' under a minute\", () => {\n    const now = new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:00:00Z\");\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:59:30Z\"), now)).toBe(\"just now\");\n  });\n  it(\"crosses the hour boundary correctly\", () => {\n    const now = new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:00:00Z\");\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:00:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"60m ago\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatConfidence\", () => {\n  it(\"always renders two decimals\", () => {\n    expect(formatConfidence(0.9)).toBe(\"0.90\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/rule-trace.ts` — `deriveRuleTrace`\n\nGaps: no resolution yet (unresolved conflict), rule decided with a value, rule decided but escalated (no value → `apply` skipped even though `ruleDecided`), no rule matched and model proposed, `appliedRuleStrategy` null but `appliedRuleId` present (fallback label).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"deriveRuleTrace\", () => {\n  it(\"shows only classify when unresolved\", () => { /* resolution: null */ });\n  it(\"marks apply as ran when a rule matched and produced a value\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"marks apply as NOT ran when a rule matched but escalated (no value)\", () => { /* ruleDecided=true, proposedValue='' */ });\n  it(\"marks propose as ran when no rule matched and model proposed a value\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"falls back to appliedRuleId when appliedRuleStrategy is null\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/audit-detail.ts` — `auditDetailParts`/`auditDetailLine`/`auditNote`\n\nGaps: entirely empty `detail` (must return `[]`, not throw); `chosenValue === proposedValue` (only pushes one, not `\"X → X\"`); `chosenValue` present but `proposedValue` absent; non-string/non-number junk in `detail` (must be ignored by `str`/`num` type guards, e.g. `NaN`, `Infinity` handling via `Number.isFinite`); `previousStatus` underscore replacement (`auto_applied` → `auto-applied`).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"auditDetailParts\", () => {\n  it(\"returns empty array for unrecognized detail keys\", () => { /* {} */ });\n  it(\"omits the arrow when proposed equals chosen\", () => { /* from='X', to='X' → ['X'] not ['X → X'] */ });\n  it(\"ignores NaN/Infinity values for numeric fields\", () => { /* confidence: NaN */ });\n  it(\"replaces underscores in previousStatus\", () => { /* previousStatus: 'auto_applied' → 'was auto-applied' */ });\n  it(\"labels count with the action-specific noun\", () => { /* action: 'conflict_detected', count: 12 → '12 conflicts' */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/uuid.ts` — `isUuid`\n\nUntested. Trivial but it's a security-adjacent guard (prevents malformed route params reaching Postgres as a cast error → 500).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"isUuid\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [\"123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000\", true],\n    [\"banana\", false],\n    [\"123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-42661417400\", false],   // one char short\n    [\"123E4567-E89B-12D3-A456-426614174000\", true],   // case-insensitive\n    [\"\", false],\n  ])(\"%s -> %s\", (input, expected) => {\n    expect(isUuid(input)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/reviewer-label.ts`, `lib/cn.ts`\n\nSmall but untested. `reviewerLabel`: username wins over email wins over fallback; null user; empty-string username (falsy but not nullish — does `??` correctly fall through?).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers username over email\", () => { /* {username:'j.rao', primaryEmailAddress:{emailAddress:'x@y.com'}} */ });\n  it(\"falls back to email when no username\", () => { /* username: null */ });\n  it(\"falls back to the provided id when user is null\", () => { /* reviewerLabel(null, 'user_123') */ });\n  it(\"treats an empty-string username as absent\", () => {\n    // BUG RISK: `user?.username ?? ...` does NOT fall through on \"\", only null/undefined\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"x@y.com\" } }, \"fallback\"))\n      .toBe(\"\"); // document actual behavior — likely NOT what's intended\n  });\n});\n```\nThis last case is worth flagging: `??` won't skip an empty-string username, so a Clerk user with `username: \"\"` would render a blank label instead of falling back to email. Worth a real test to pin down intended behavior.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Zod-adjacent pure functions in `types/*.ts`\n\n### `types/queue.ts` — `conflictFieldLabel`, `severityReason`\n\nGaps: `duplicate` where `from === to` (no `→`, falls to `\"duplicate record\"`), `duplicate` where one side has 0 values, `orphan` with `childCount === 1` (singular \"child\" vs plural \"children\"), `default` branch severity 3 vs other.\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"conflictFieldLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"labels orphan rows as 'entity absent'\", () => {});\n  it(\"shows N -> M for duplicates with different counts\", () => {});\n  it(\"shows 'duplicate record' when both sides have equal counts\", () => {});\n  it(\"falls back to the field name for a plain field conflict\", () => {});\n});\n\ndescribe(\"severityReason\", () => {\n  it(\"pluralizes children correctly for childCount=1 vs >1\", () => {\n    // 'has 1 child' vs 'has 2 children'\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `types/run.ts` — `isTerminalRunStatus`, `runStageIndex`, `isStatKnown`, `failedStage`\n\nGaps: `failedStage` regex matching — case-insensitivity, unknown verb (returns `null`, not throws), no `stage=` at all, `error: null`; `isStatKnown` for a `failed` run (special-cased to always `true` per the comment — this is a business rule worth pinning); stat produced exactly at its own stage boundary (`runStageIndex(status) > runStageIndex(produced)`, not `>=`).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"failedStage\", () => {\n  it(\"parses stage= case-insensitively\", () => { expect(failedStage(\"... STAGE=Extract\")).toBe(\"extracting\"); });\n  it(\"returns null for an unrecognized verb\", () => { expect(failedStage(\"stage=teleport\")).toBeNull(); });\n  it(\"returns null when error is null\", () => { expect(failedStage(null)).toBeNull(); });\n  it(\"returns null when no stage= marker exists\", () => { expect(failedStage(\"connection refused\")).toBeNull(); });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isStatKnown\", () => {\n  it(\"is always true for a failed run regardless of stage\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"tokensUsed\", \"failed\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"is false for a stat whose producing stage hasn't completed\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"extracting\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"is exactly false at the producing stage itself (strict >)\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"matching\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `types/resolution.ts` — `isHumanDecided`\n\nTrivial but untested boundary check: `auto_applied`/`escalated`/`proposed` must all be `false`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Server business logic — needs DB fixture/mock\n\nThese currently have **zero** tests and carry the most business risk (money-adjacent: audit trail integrity, review actions, export correctness). They need either a real Postgres test DB (recommended — Drizzle + testcontainers/pglite) or `getDb()` mocked. I'd prioritize integration tests over mocking Drizzle's query builder, since the value here is in the SQL logic (joins, filters, ordering), not just the TS.\n\n### `lib/server/conflicts.ts` — `recordReview` (highest priority: this is the write path with the anti-hallucination guard duplicated from `validate-value.ts`)\n\nMissing scenarios:\n- `conflictId` doesn't exist → 404\n- Conflict exists but resolution is `null` (run still resolving) → 409\n- `approve` action when `proposedValue` is empty (rule said escalate) → 409, explicit message\n- `override` with a value not in `observed` → 400, delegates to `checkObservedValue`\n- `override` with a valid value → `overrideValue` set, `chosenValue` = folded match, status = `overridden`\n- `reject` action → `chosenValue` recorded as `null` in audit detail even though `resolution.proposedValue` exists (this is an explicit \"not overriding a rejection with a value\" branch — easy to regress)\n- Every action appends exactly one audit row with the *previous* status captured correctly\n- Moving *off* an override (e.g. re-reviewing) clears `overrideValue` — the comment says this but there's no path shown for re-review; worth confirming current behavior with a test since it's asserted in a code comment\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/conflicts.test.ts (integration — needs seeded run/conflict/resolution rows)\ndescribe(\"recordReview\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 404 for a nonexistent conflict\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns 409 when the conflict has no resolution yet\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns 409 approving a conflict with an empty proposedValue\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns 400 overriding with a value not in observed\", async () => {});\n  it(\"records an override's chosen value as the folded observed match, not the raw input\", async () => {});\n  it(\"records chosenValue as null in audit detail on reject, even though a proposal exists\", async () => {});\n  it(\"captures previousStatus in the audit detail correctly\", async () => {});\n  it(\"clears overrideValue when a reviewer moves off a prior override\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/conflicts.ts` — `getQueuePage`/`toQueueRow`\n\nMissing: orphan where side A absent (`present: false`, identity falls to B); orphan where the \"absent\" side actually has stray non-empty values (defensive case); `sourceName` for a source belonging to neither run source (`\"unknown source\"` fallback — this masks an engine bug, worth asserting it doesn't throw); pagination `pageCount` when `total === 0` (must be `1`, not `0`, per `Math.max(1, ...)`); tiebreak ordering stability across two pages.\n\n### `lib/server/rulesets.ts` — `createRulesetVersion`\n\nMissing: concurrent creates for the same name don't produce duplicate version numbers (the advisory-lock behavior — hard to unit test without real concurrency, but worth an integration test spawning two concurrent calls); first version for a brand-new name starts at 1 (`highest ?? 0) + 1`); creating a new version deactivates *all* previously active rulesets across *every* name, not just the same name (re-read the code — `tx.update(rulesets).set({isActive:false}).where(eq(rulesets.isActive, true))` has no `name` filter, meaning saving ruleset \"B\" as v2 deactivates active ruleset \"A\" too — **this looks like it could be an actual bug** worth flagging, not just a test gap).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"createRulesetVersion\", () => {\n  it(\"starts a new ruleset name at version 1\", async () => {});\n  it(\"increments version per-name\", async () => {});\n  it(\"deactivates the previous active version of the SAME name\", async () => {});\n  it(\"BUG CHECK: verify it does not also deactivate an active ruleset of a DIFFERENT name\", async () => {\n    // Given ruleset \"A\" v2 active and ruleset \"B\" v1 active simultaneously (if that's\n    // ever a valid state), saving a new version of \"A\" should not touch \"B\".\n    // Current code's WHERE clause has no name filter — confirm intended behavior.\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/runs.ts` — `failUndispatchedRun`\n\nMissing: guard on `status = \"queued\"` — must be a no-op once the engine has advanced the run past `queued` (i.e., calling it on a `matching` run must not overwrite progress). This is the one place where a race between engine progress and web-layer failure-handling is explicitly guarded, and it's untested.\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"failUndispatchedRun\", () => {\n  it(\"marks a queued run as failed\", async () => {});\n  it(\"does NOT overwrite a run the engine has already advanced past queued\", async () => {\n    // seed run with status=\"matching\", call failUndispatchedRun, assert unchanged\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/export.ts` — `applyDecisions`, `appliedValue`, `decisionsToCsv`, `estimateExportBytes`, `getExportSizing`\n\nMissing:\n- `appliedValue`: every status branch — `proposed`/`escalated`/`rejected` → `null`; `overridden` → `overrideValue` not `proposedValue`; `auto_applied`/`approved` → `proposedValue`\n- `applyDecisions`: `reparented` flag true only when resolved parent differs from original; a decision on a field other than `parentExternalId` must not affect hierarchy; a decision with `appliedValue === null` (rejected/escalated) must not override the account's original parent\n- `decisionsToCsv`: CSV injection/escaping — values containing commas, quotes, `\\r\\n`; `null` fields render as empty string not `\"null\"`\n- `csvCell`/`isExportSection`: unknown section string rejected\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"appliedValue\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [\"proposed\", \"X\", null, null],\n    [\"escalated\", \"X\", null, null],\n    [\"rejected\", \"X\", null, null],\n    [\"auto_applied\", \"X\", null, \"X\"],\n    [\"approved\", \"X\", null, \"X\"],\n    [\"overridden\", \"X\", \"Y\", \"Y\"],\n  ])(\"status=%s proposed=%s override=%s -> %s\", (status, proposed, override, expected) => {\n    expect(appliedValue(status, proposed, override)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"applyDecisions\", () => {\n  it(\"marks reparented=true only when the resolved parent differs from original\", () => {});\n  it(\"ignores decisions on fields other than parentExternalId\", () => {});\n  it(\"does not change parent when appliedValue is null (escalated/rejected)\", () => {});\n});\n\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv\", () => {\n  it(\"escapes values containing commas, quotes, and newlines\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([{ ...base, entityName: 'Acme, \"The\" Co\\nLine2' } as any]);\n    expect(csv).toContain('\"Acme, \"\"The\"\" Co\\nLine2\"');\n  });\n  it(\"renders null fields as empty cells, not the string 'null'\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/audit.ts` — `getAuditPage`, `auditFilters`\n\nMissing: `byAction` counts must ignore the `action` filter itself but respect `runId` (mirrors the \"omit own facet\" pattern in conflicts.ts — same bug class if regressed); tiebreak ordering (`createdAt` then `id` desc) prevents duplicate rows across pages when multiple entries share a timestamp; `page` clamped to minimum 1 for `page=0` or negative input.\n\n### `lib/server/entities.ts` — `countChildrenByParent`\n\nMissing: empty `externalIds` array short-circuits to empty Map without querying (`if (parents.length === 0) return new Map()`); duplicate ids in input are de-duped (`[...new Set(...)]`); empty-string ids filtered out before querying.\n\n### `lib/server/engine.ts` — `startRun`, `fetchEngineStatus`\n\nMissing (needs `fetch` mocking, e.g. `msw` or `vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", ...)`):\n- `ENGINE_URL` unset → throws `EngineUnreachableError` before any fetch\n- fetch throws (network error) → wrapped in `EngineUnreachableError`\n- fetch times out (`AbortSignal.timeout`) → error message says \"no response within Ns\"\n- non-ok response → error includes truncated body (300 chars)\n- ok response with wrong-shaped JSON body → `EngineUnreachableError`, not a silent pass\n- `fetchEngineStatus`: any failure (network, non-ok, bad schema) returns `null`, never throws — this is the important contract (polling degrades gracefully)\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"startRun\", () => {\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when ENGINE_URL is unset\", async () => {});\n  it(\"wraps a network failure in EngineUnreachableError\", async () => {});\n  it(\"wraps a non-ok response, truncating the body to 300 chars\", async () => {});\n  it(\"throws when the 200 response body fails schema validation\", async () => {});\n});\n\ndescribe(\"fetchEngineStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (never throws) on network failure\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns null on non-ok status\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns null when the body fails schema validation\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns the parsed status on success\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/auth.ts` — `requireReviewer`, `getReviewer`\n\nMissing (mock `@clerk/nextjs/server`):\n- `auth.protect()` having \"succeeded\" but `userId` still missing → throws explicitly (defensive contract-break guard, currently unexercised)\n- `getReviewer()` returns `null` when unauthenticated, without calling `requireReviewer`/redirecting\n- `getReviewer()` delegates to `requireReviewer` (and thus `reviewerLabel`) when authenticated\n\n---\n\n## 4. API routes — request/response contract tests\n\nNone of these have integration tests (e.g. via `next/test` or hitting the route handler function directly with a mock `Request`).\n\n### `app/api/runs/route.ts` POST — most complex handler, zero coverage\n\nGaps: `sourceAId === sourceBId` → 400 before any DB call; nonexistent `sourceAId`/`sourceBId` → 400 with which-side-specific message; nonexistent `rulesetId` → 400; **the engine-dispatch-failure path** — run row created, audit `run_started` appended, `startRun` throws `EngineUnreachableError`, response is still `201` (not 500) with `failUndispatchedRun` + `run_failed` audit both called; a non-`EngineUnreachableError` thrown from `startRun` is *rethrown*, not swallowed (currently unexercised — `if (!(cause instanceof EngineUnreachableError)) throw cause;`).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"POST /api/runs\", () => {\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId equals sourceBId\", async () => {});\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId does not exist\", async () => {});\n  it(\"400s when rulesetId does not exist\", async () => {});\n  it(\"still returns 201 when the engine is unreachable, with the run marked failed\", async () => {\n    // mock startRun to throw EngineUnreachableError\n    // assert response.status === 201\n    // assert run row status === \"failed\", error contains \"stage=dispatch\"\n    // assert a run_failed audit row was appended\n  });\n  it(\"rethrows a non-EngineUnreachableError from startRun instead of swallowing it\", async () => {});\n  it(\"appends a run_started audit row with reviewer as actor, not the request body\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n### `app/api/conflicts/route.ts` GET\n\nGaps: invalid query params (bad `severities`, out-of-range `page`) → 400 via zod issue message; `state: \"no-runs\"` → returns the specific empty shape `{run:null, conflicts:[], total:0, counts:null}`, not a 404; requires auth (unauthenticated → whatever `requireReviewer` does, redirect/404) — not exercised at the route level.\n\n### `app/api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution/route.ts` PATCH\n\nGaps: non-UUID `conflictId` param → 404 *before* touching the DB or auth (order matters — currently `isUuid` check precedes `requireReviewer`... actually re-check: `isUuid` check is first, then `parseJson`, then `requireReviewer` — so an unauthenticated request with a bad body still gets validated before auth is checked, which may or may not be intended); invalid body shape (e.g. `action: \"delete\"`) → 400 from `parseJson`; `recordReview` returning each of 400/404/409 → route maps status code correctly.\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"PATCH /api/conflicts/:conflictId/resolution\", () => {\n  it(\"404s for a non-UUID conflictId without touching auth or DB\", async () => {});\n  it(\"400s for a malformed action body\", async () => {});\n  it(\"maps recordReview's ok:false code straight through to the response status\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns reviewedBy from the session, not the request body\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n### `app/api/runs/[runId]/export/route.ts` GET\n\nGaps: `parseSections` — unknown section name → 400; empty `sections=` (empty string after split/filter) → 400 not \"use default\"; duplicate sections in query (`sections=hierarchy,hierarchy`) → de-duped in canonical order; `format` other than `json`/`csv` → 400; csv format ignores `orphans`/`stats`/`hierarchy` sections entirely (only decisions ever go to CSV) — worth an explicit test since it's an easy silent-drop bug.\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"parseSections / GET export\", () => {\n  it(\"400s on an unknown section name\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s on an empty sections string\", () => {});\n  it(\"de-dupes and canonically orders sections regardless of input order\", () => {\n    // sections=decisions,hierarchy,decisions -> [hierarchy, decisions]\n  });\n  it(\"400s on format other than json/csv\", async () => {});\n  it(\"csv format ignores non-decisions sections silently — pin this down explicitly\", async () => {\n    // request ?format=csv&sections=hierarchy,orphans,stats — assert response is still\n    // decisions-shaped CSV (currently empty, since decisions wasn't requested) rather than erroring\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `app/api/audit/export/route.ts` GET\n\nGaps: bad `runId` (non-UUID) → 404; `runId` for a nonexistent run → 404; invalid `action` → 400; CSV escaping of `detail` JSON containing commas/quotes; empty entries list still produces a valid header-only CSV.\n\n### `app/api/_lib/respond.ts` — `parseJson`, `fieldIssues`\n\nGaps: non-JSON body (`request.json()` throws) → 400 \"Body must be JSON.\"; zod failure → `issues` keyed by dotted path (`\"config.objects\"`); a root-level issue (empty path) → keyed as `\"_\"`.\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"parseJson\", () => {\n  it(\"400s with 'Body must be JSON.' when the body isn't valid JSON\", async () => {});\n  it(\"keys field issues by dotted path\", async () => {});\n  it(\"keys a root-level issue as '_'\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Client-side: `components/conflicts/use-review.ts`\n\nNo component/hook tests exist (`@testing-library/react-hooks` or `renderHook` from RTL). Gaps: `submit` sets `pendingId` during the request and clears it after, even on failure; failed request leaves `decided` untouched (no optimistic rollback needed, per the comment — worth pinning as a regression guard); successful request updates `decided[conflictId]` and triggers `router.refresh()` inside a transition; two rapid `submit` calls for different conflicts don't clobber each other's `pendingId` (currently a single `pendingId`, not a Set — worth confirming intended single-flight-per-hook behavior).\n\n```ts\n// components/conflicts/use-review.test.tsx\nimport { renderHook, act } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { vi, describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ useRouter: () => ({ refresh: vi.fn() }) }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/api-client\");\n\ndescribe(\"useReview\", () => {\n  it(\"sets pendingId during the request and clears it after success\", async () => {});\n  it(\"sets pendingId during the request and clears it after failure\", async () => {});\n  it(\"does not update `decided` on a failed submit\", async () => {});\n  it(\"updates decided[conflictId] with the server's status/reviewedBy on success\", async () => {});\n  it(\"calls router.refresh() only on success, not on failure\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Missing error-handling coverage (cross-cutting)\n\n| Area | Untested failure mode |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/server/engine.ts` | Engine timeout, malformed response body, ENGINE_URL missing |\n| `app/api/runs/route.ts` | Engine dispatch failure leaving run in recoverable `failed` state instead of throwing 500 |\n| `lib/server/conflicts.ts` `recordReview` | Invented override value rejected before any write |\n| `app/api/_lib/respond.ts` | Non-JSON request body |\n| `lib/server/auth.ts` | Clerk contract break (`protect()` succeeds but no `userId`) |\n| `lib/server/rulesets.ts` | Concurrent version creation (race on advisory lock) |\n| All route handlers | Unauthenticated request behavior isn't verified anywhere — `requireReviewer()` is trusted but never exercised through a route in a test |\n\n## 7. Integration test gaps\n\n- **Full review flow**: create run → seed conflict/resolution → PATCH review action → assert `resolutions` row *and* `audit_log` row both updated in one transaction-equivalent check. No test currently exercises `conflicts.ts` + `audit.ts` together.\n- **Export end-to-end**: `buildRunExport` → `decisionsToCsv`/JSON serialization, verifying a value that changes shape between `DecisionRow` and CSV round-trips correctly (e.g. `null` vs `undefined` vs empty string).\n- **Queue ↔ ruleset versioning**: a resolution's `appliedRuleId` resolving to a strategy from the *run's* ruleset version, not the currently active one — this cross-cuts `conflicts.ts` and `rulesets.ts` and has no test proving old runs stay stable after a ruleset is superseded.\n- **Run status polling fallback**: `app/api/runs/[runId]/status/route.ts` preferring engine response over DB row for non-terminal runs, falling back to DB row when engine is unreachable — needs an integration test with a mocked engine.\n- **Proxy/middleware**: `proxy.ts`'s matcher regex has no test proving which paths it does/doesn't cover (e.g. does a `.pdf` or `.json` static asset incorrectly fall through to middleware since they're absent from the exclusion list?).\n\n---\n\n**Recommended order of attack**: `lib/validate-value.ts` and `lib/server/conflicts.ts::recordReview` first (correctness-critical write path with duplicated validation logic across two layers), then `lib/server/export.ts::appliedValue`/`applyDecisions` (silent data-correctness bugs are easy to ship there), then the API route contract tests, then the pure formatters/derivers last (safe, but cheap wins for regression-proofing the UI).\n",
